([Abstract]) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 702 Tm
(FlashAttention: Fast and Memory-Efficient Exact Attention with IO-Awareness) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 669 Tm
(Authors: Tri Dao, Daniel Y. Fu, Stefano Ermon, Atri Rudra, Christopher Re \(2022\)) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 636 Tm
(Abstract: Transformers are slow and memory-hungry on long sequences, since the time) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 621 Tm
(and memory complexity of self-attention are quadratic in sequence length.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 606 Tm
(Approximate attention methods have attempted to address this problem by trading off) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 591 Tm
(model quality to reduce the compute complexity, but often do not achieve wall-clock) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 576 Tm
(speedup.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 543 Tm
(We argue that a missing principle is making attention algorithms IO-aware-that is,) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 528 Tm
(carefully accounting for reads and writes between levels of GPU memory. We propose) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 513 Tm
(FlashAttention, an IO-aware exact attention algorithm that uses tiling to reduce the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 498 Tm
(number of memory reads/writes between GPU high bandwidth memory \(HBM\) and GPU) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 483 Tm
(on-chip SRAM.) Tj
ET
endstream
